{title: 294 - Power in the Blood}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Bb]Would you be free from the [Eb]burden of [Bb]sin?
[F]There's pow'r in the [Bb]blood, pow'r in the blood;
[Bb]Would you o'er evil [Eb]a [Bb]victory [F7]win?
[Bb]There's wonderful power in the blood.

Refrain:
[Eb]There is pow'r, pow'r, [Bb]wonder [F]working [Gm]pow'r
[Dm]In the [Bb]blood of the Lamb;
[Bb]There is [Eb]pow'r, pow'r, wonder [Bb]working [F]pow'r
[F7]In the precious blood of the [Bb]Lamb.

Verse 2:
[Bb]Would be free from your [Eb]passion and [Bb]pride?
[F]There's pow'r in the [Bb]blood, pow'r in the blood;
[Bb]Come for a cleansing [Eb]to [Bb]Calvary's [F7]tide?
[Bb]There's wonderful power in the blood.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Would you do service for [Eb]Jesus your [Bb]King?
[F]There's pow'r in the [Bb]blood, pow'r in the blood;
[Bb]Would you live daily [Eb]His [Bb]praises [F]to [F7]sing?
[Bb]There's wonderful power in the blood.
